    "body": "Readings for #1928 (issue-worker-high, branch `issue/1928-stock-open-run-offset`).\n\n**Cause.** In `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`, the Contour selection arm sends an open run to `machining2d::contour_along_chain(run, &cp)` when `part_solid_of` is false. `part_solid_of` is false when a pick is on the stock entity. `contour_along_chain` rides the points of the run. Thus the tool centre was on the picked line. Commit 64c822fec added this centreline pass. `docs/decisions/1777-contour-open-run-side.md` kept it for stock picks.\n\n**Before the fix (main d1484f02a).** Test fixture: part 40 x 40 x 10, stock 70 x 70 x 10, tool D10 (R = 5). Pick: the north edge of the stock (y = 35).\n\n- Side Auto: the feed moves are 0.0000 mm (min) to 0.0000 mm (max) from the line. The tool centre is on y = 35 at Z10 and Z0.\n- Stock to leave 0.5, Side Outside: 0.0000 / 0.0000 mm.\n- No part in the setup, Side Auto: the path is generated on the line. There is no refusal.\n- Stock 44 x 44, Side Inside: the path is generated on y = 22 with 3 warnings. There is no refusal.\n\n**After the fix.**\n\n- Side Auto and Side Outside: the tool centre is on y = 40 (+R). Side Inside: y = 30 (-R). Min and max distance are 5.000 mm, within 0.001 mm. There are 0 warnings.\n- Stock to leave 0.5: the distance is 5.500 mm.\n- No part, Side Auto: refused by name. The message tells the user to choose Inside or Outside.\n- Stock 44 x 44, Side Inside: refused by name (\"cuts the part\"). Side Auto is cut.\n\n**Callers of `contour_along_chain`.**\n\n1. `generate.rs`, Contour selection arm (stock runs): changed. It now calls the new `machining2d::contour_open_run_sided`.\n2. `contour_open.rs` `open_pass` (open Boundary): not changed. Containment already offsets the run.\n3. `contour_run_side.rs` `contour_open_run` (#1777, part runs): not changed. Its fallback (no part material beside the run at any level) still rides the line, with a note.\n4. Motion tests of the primitive: not changed.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
